From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: leave the unused fq alone when purging a txq of a HAS_TX_QUEUE driver

With HAS_TX_QUEUE (785) the driver queues the frames itself:
ieee80211_txq_setup_flows() returns before fq_init(), so local->fq and
its lock are never set up, and nothing is ever queued on a txq. The
interfaces still get their txqs, though, and ieee80211_txq_purge(),
called when one stops or goes away, took the uninitialised fq->lock to
empty a queue that cannot hold anything. It only worked because the
memory is zeroed; lockdep reports it ("trying to register non-static
key", ieee80211_txq_purge from ieee80211_do_stop, ath11k with NSS
offload on IPQ5018) and turns itself off.

Skip the fq part of the purge with HAS_TX_QUEUE, as
ieee80211_txq_teardown_flows() and ieee80211_queue_skb() already do.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -1560,10 +1560,16 @@
 	struct fq *fq = &local->fq;
 	struct fq_tin *tin = &txqi->tin;
 
-	spin_lock_bh(&fq->lock);
-	fq_tin_reset(fq, tin, fq_skb_free_func);
-	ieee80211_purge_tx_queue(&local->hw, &txqi->frags);
-	spin_unlock_bh(&fq->lock);
+	/* With HAS_TX_QUEUE the driver queues the frames itself: fq was
+	 * never set up (no fq_init(), so not even its lock) and nothing
+	 * was ever queued on this txq.
+	 */
+	if (!ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, HAS_TX_QUEUE)) {
+		spin_lock_bh(&fq->lock);
+		fq_tin_reset(fq, tin, fq_skb_free_func);
+		ieee80211_purge_tx_queue(&local->hw, &txqi->frags);
+		spin_unlock_bh(&fq->lock);
+	}
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&local->active_txq_lock[txqi->txq.ac]);
 	list_del_init(&txqi->schedule_order);
